questiontext.text:
        In Java, what happens with the statements inside the braces of an <code>if</code> statement?<br><br>
        <pre><code>if (condition) {
    // statements
}</code></pre>

        Consider:<br><br>
        <pre><code>if (x &gt; 0);
{
    doSomething();
}</code></pre>
        What is the effect of the semicolon after the <code>if</code>?

        In a method like:<br><br>
        <pre><code>public void insertMoney(int amount) {
    if (amount &gt; 0) {
        balance = balance + amount;
    } else {
        System.out.printf("Use a positive amount: %d%n", amount);
    }
}</code></pre>
        What is the primary purpose of the <code>if</code> check?

        Given:<br><br>
        <pre><code>// do some work
if (flag) {
    process();
}
// more work here</code></pre>
        What can you say about the “more work here” section?
